35367/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335367" :question/id #uuid "04ed6984-51d2-56a0-9687-075ebc560f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335367" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\sqrt[3]{x+y-1}+z,\\, & y(0)=2 \\\\ {z}^{′}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-1}{w+1},\\, & z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′}=\\sqrt{x+{z}^{2}}-y,\\, & w(0)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with one step to approximate $y(1),$ $z(1),$ and $w(1).$\n\n$\\,y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(1)≈$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,w(1)≈$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$, $z$ and $w$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we place the initial condition data in a table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},$ ${z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt[3]{x+y-1}+z \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{0+2-1}+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-1}{w+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {w}^{′} & =\\sqrt{x+{z}^{2}}-y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+{1}^{2}}-2 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ |  | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |  | $1$ | $-1$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+2=4 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+(-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n| $1$ | $4$ |  |  | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(1)≈4,$\n$z(1)≈\\frac{5}{2},$\nand\n$w(1)≈0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335367/field-1" "q-335367/field-2" "q-335367/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8b20277-7fb3-5702-a295-1b1722d1cc5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335155/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8e9d6218-bd00-5069-98fc-fef46f11fd48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335155/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3c5e6ac-71e4-5b53-a82d-fc92ef739d48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335155/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71