| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z(1)≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w(1)≈$\n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nFirst, because the initial conditions are $y(0)=1,$ $z(0)=2,$ and $w(0)=1,$ we place $y=1,$ $z=2,$ and $w=1$ in the table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  | $2$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},{z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+y+{w}^{2} \\\\  & =0+1+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2y-z \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1-2 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {w}^{′} & =-w+xz \\\\  & =-1+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |  | $2$ | $0$ |  | $1$ | $-1$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=2\\cdot 1=2 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx=(-1)\\cdot 1=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+2=3 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=2+0=2 \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+(-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ |\n| $1$ | $3$ |  |  | $2$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(1)≈3,$\n$z(1)≈2,$\nand\n$w(1)≈0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335155/field-1" "q-335155/field-2" "q-335155/field-3" "q-335155/field-4" "q-335155/field-5" "q-335155/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8b20277-7fb3-5702-a295-1b1722d1cc5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335155"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "458f1310-9327-5b78-96eb-271b14226f65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b83decb6-5856-5b56-a0fe-866c55034007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e00d7a6e-e449-5a41-9830-43b353809e28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335290/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-335290/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-335290/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "43c0533a-3b3d-501b-8ed5-fec069637853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "527ccc9a-96d1-5b6b-8193-95d1a4b4f002" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335290/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-335290/field-2/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "45dbd4c3-0f60-5b58-899a-cd4b6d98f582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d73a515-8b1f-5b1a-b716-5ed2fb34f2a4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335290/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-335290/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335290" :question/id #uuid "3c328467-0945-5703-9ef4-7d7d1a77142b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335290" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=y+z+w,\\, & y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′}=xy-{w}^{2},\\, & z(0)=-2 \\\\ {w}^{′}=\\frac{yz}{w},\\, & w(0)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with one step to approximate $y\\,(\\frac{1}{2}),$ $z\\,(\\frac{1}{2}),$ and $w\\,(\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n$\\,y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,w\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nSince we want to find the values of $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ at $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1}{2}-0=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we place the initial condition data in a table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  | $-2$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},$ ${z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+z+w \\\\  & =1+(-2)+1 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =xy-{w}^{2} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {w}^{′} & =\\frac{yz}{w} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)}{1} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |  | $-2$ | $-1$ |  | $1$ | $-2$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-2+(-\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+(-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |  |  | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈1,\\,z\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈-\\frac{5}{2},\\,w\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-335290/field-1" "q-335290/field-2" "q-335290/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8b20277-7fb3-5702-a295-1b1722d1cc5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335310/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a939e851-cf9a-5a1a-be28-c5170e554a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335310/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f175473b-ecaf-52d5-9684-08fe3c4d2f5d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335310/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-335310/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335310/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bfffc976-4315-5de6-87cf-7a86c5c6bb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335310/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc8a42f-3d28-5921-8376-1163d921ba75" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335310/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-335310/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335310/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b113eb16-9de1-5eab-845d-a2c6cb